# Cosmic muon run.
#
#   MuonSim -n 10000 -o cosmic.root macro/cosmic_muon.mac
#   MuonSim -n 100 -s 12345 macro/cosmic_muon.mac      reproducible
#
# Why a sphere, how the launch point is built, how to pick R, and what to check:
# doc/cosmic_sphere.pdf. Command syntax: doc/generator.md. Numbers are deliberately
# NOT repeated here -- the flux file is regenerated from time to time, and a rate
# written into a macro goes stale silently. The run prints what it read.

/run/initialize

/run/verbose 1
/event/verbose 0
/tracking/verbose 0

# --- what to save ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Bits: 1 heavy, 2 non-shower e±, 4 gamma, 8 shower e±, 16 optical. A step needs
# its bit in BOTH masks. Gammas are off deliberately: see README.

/ROOT/savetrackopt 1
/ROOT/savestepopt 1
/ROOT/savehitphoton 1

# --- the source -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The SPHERE flux file, holding the TH3D h_flux. The plane file is a different
# normalisation and would be wrong here.
#
# Pick one. (a) is the whole rock shell, needed if muon-induced neutrons matter.
# (b) is the smallest sphere around the apparatus, for muons hitting the detector
# only -- it loses neutrons made in the far floor and walls.
#
# (b)'s centre and radius follow from the geometry, so moving the water tank
# (geo::frame::kTopZ) means recomputing them.

# (a) whole rock shell
#/gen/vertex cosmic input amore_muon_flux_sphere.root sphere 0 0 0 16400 mm

# (b) apparatus only
/gen/vertex cosmic input /home/cupsoft/Works/MuonFlux/muonflux_ug/run/amore/amore_muon_flux_sphere.root sphere 0 0 3846 5944 mm

# /gen/list

/run/beamOn {nevent}
